Description: Monte Carlo Particle Lists (Python)
 MCPL is a binary file format for lists of particle state information, for
 storing particles and exchanging them between Monte Carlo simulation codes.
 .
 This package contains the MCPL Python module.

Package: mcpl
Architecture: any
Depends: python3-mcpl (= ${source:Version}),
         libmcpl-dev (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: python3-matplotlib (>= 3.6), python3-tk
Suggests: mcpl-extra
Description: Monte Carlo Particle Lists
 MCPL is a binary file format for lists of particle state information, for
 storing particles and exchanging them between Monte Carlo simulation codes.
 .
 This package contains the command-line tools mcpltool and mcpl-config, and
 depends on the MCPL library, headers, and Python module.

Package: mcpl-extra
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Monte Carlo Particle Lists (converters for MCNP and PHITS)
 MCPL is a binary file format for lists of particle state information, for
 storing particles and exchanging them between Monte Carlo simulation codes.
 .
 This package contains the converters between MCPL files and the SSW files of
 MCNP (ssw2mcpl and mcpl2ssw), and the dump files of PHITS (phits2mcpl and
 mcpl2phits).
